      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DOUBLE LOU (1) was a beaten favourite last week but it was his first outing for three-and-a-half months and he worked from a wide barrier so the effort to box on for a 1.5m second had plenty of merit. Owns a strong second-up record so will be improved and won the 3CG final of this series last year. He looks much better served by the ace draw. FOREVER ONTHE PUNT (2) has been terrific in winning all three starts at this circuit since joining Brad Hewitt for this campaign. Came from this barrier when he scored over this distance last week. Could add to the winning streak. WICKED WIZARD (4) took his record at this circuit and distance to three from four when beating DOUBLE LOU last week. He draws to play a role again. JUNGLE DRAGON (6) hasn't been far from the placegetters of late and his best form would measure right up. SINALOA (5) improved to place last week and is a two-time third-up winner so could progress further aided by a good draw.",
